Much simpler calculations get to the same conclusion.

When one has already protection in range 9-19 then there is a one in the 
current protection chance for getting an additional point for your money.

The amount to pay is 400*XL and n is your current protection: You pay it 
once and get your point or you pay twice (1-1/n chance) and get your 
point or you pay thrice ((1-1/n)^2 chance) and get your point etc.

Mathematically:

400*XL*sum(i=0..oo)((1-1/n)^i) = 400*XL*(1/(1-(1-1/n))) =
400*XL*(1/(1-1+1/n)) = 400*XL*(1/(1/n)) = 400*XL*n

So the average amount you pay for additional protection when your 
protection already is in range 9-19 is 400 times your level times your 
current protection.

